      "writtenOn": "2020-03-19T23:48:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the original code, I see\n\n \t\tclock_flash_latency(FLASH_ACLK_64MHZ);\n\nwhere FLASH_ACLK_64MHZ is\n\n  /* Flash latency settings for AHB/ACLK at 64 Mhz and Vcore in VOS1 range */\n#define FLASH_ACLK_64MHZ (STM32_FLASH_ACR_WRHIGHFREQ_85MHZ | \\\n\t\t\t  (0 \u003c\u003c STM32_FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_SHIFT))\n\nwhich looks like the comment is correct (using the right flash latency setting for VOS1, but not VOS3)\n\nbut then the code sets to VOS3 like you mentioned:\n\n  \t\tswitch_voltage_scale(STM32_PWR_D3CR_VOS3);\n\nSo that does seem like the old code was wrong.\n\nIf I\u0027m reading the table in https://www.st.com/resource/en/reference_manual/dm00314099-stm32h742-stm32h743-753-and-stm32h750-value-line-advanced-arm-based-32-bit-mcus-stmicroelectronics.pdf#page\u003d159 correctly you need to change to 1 WS in clock_flash_latency. You can fix it in a followup CL since that will make the history easier to read (no functional change in this commit). It\u0027s not an optimization though; I think it\u0027s a bug in this case since it is set to zero wait states, but should be set to one at that voltage.",
